  </div></section>
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#F6F3EE;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 10px;">Is White Rock Fence Co a fence contractor?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">No. It is an advertising site for independent Dallas-area fence contractors. It does not build, repair or install fences or gates, and it does not hold a contractor license. The contractor who quotes your job in writing is the one who does the work, so read the quote and the contract with that contractor in mind.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 10px;">Does Texas license fence contractors, and what should I ask for?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">We did not find a state license category for fence contractors, so Texas does not license them at the state level. Some cities do register contractors, including Dallas, Richardson and Irving, and Dallas asks for a general contractor on a fence permit application. Ask each contractor for their city registration where it applies and for proof of insurance, and confirm the details with the City.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 10px;">Are the prices on this site a quote?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">No. Prices on this site are figures that independent firms or national guides publish, shown with their source. For example, one DFW firm advertises installed cedar privacy fence at $18 to $28 per linear foot for a standard 6-foot height, and another advertises $30 to $60 for 6-foot wood. Your price depends on height, style, gates, access and removal of the old fence, so call now and get two or three written quotes for the same scope.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="background:linear-gradient(135deg, #2A3035 0%, #3A4147 50%, #2A3035 100%);padding:64px 24px;text-align:center;">
  <h2 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,40px);font-weight:800;color:#fff;margin-bottom:16px;">Fence or Gate Trouble in Dallas? Call and Talk It Through.</h2>
  <p style="font-size:16px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);margin-bottom:28px;max-width:520px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;">Written quotes from independent Dallas fence contractors.</p>
  <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
    <a href="tel:+12145550137" class="btn-cream">Call Now — (214) 555-0137</a>
    <a href="/#contact" class="btn-outline-white">Get a Quote</a>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
